<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crémieux Decree</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crémieux Decree was a decree issued by the French Government of National Defence on 24 October 1870, named after the justice minister Adolphe Crémieux. It granted French citizenship to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, while Muslim Algerians remained subjects without full citizenship, a distinction that deepened divisions in the colony. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> regime revoked it in 1940, and it was restored in 1943.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cremieux-decree.jpg" alt="Crémieux Decree" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Profburp at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cremieux_136.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
